      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Gloria Leonard''' (born [[August 28]], [[1940]] in [[The Bronx]], [[New York]], [[USA]]) was an [[erotic actress]] who later became a magazine publisher. She is sometimes credited as:
'''C. Gale Leonard''' or '''Gail Leonard'''.

Her physical measurements are 40-33-37 and 5' 9&quot;. She has brown hair with gold highlights and brown eyes. She performed in [[pornography|hardcore]] from the mid '70's and was in some of the movies that are considered to be classics of early [[pornography]], including ''The Trouble With Young Stuff'', ''[[All About Gloria Leonard]]'' and ''[[The Opening of Misty Beethoven]]''. She worked with [[Constance Money]], [[Leslie Bovee]], [[Sharon Mitchell]], [[Jennifer Welles]], [[Samantha Fox (Porn actress)|Samantha Fox]] before retiring from the screen in the early 80's. She is a member of [[XRCO|X-Rated Critics Organization]] (XRCO) and the [[AVN Award|(AVN) Halls of Fame]] .

Leonard served as publisher of ''[[High Society (magazine)|High Society]]'' for 14 years, introducing for the first time such features as nude [[celebrit]]ies and [[phone sex]]. 

She currently lives on a tropical island, where her hobbies include playing chess, working out, and relaxing at the beach.

