  <page>
    <title>Non-commercial educational</title>
    <id>275673</id>
    <revision>
      <id>33998736</id>
      <timestamp>2006-01-05T18:04:16Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Krash</username>
        <id>219529</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>pipe Megahertz</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">The term '''non-commercial educational''' (NCE) applies to a [[radio station]] that does not accept or air advertisements, as defined in the [[United States|U.S.]] by the [[Federal Communications Commission|FCC]].  NCE stations do not pay licensing fees for their non-profit use of the [[radio spectrum]].

On the [[FM broadcast band]], the FCC has reserved the lowest 20 channels, 201~220 (88.1~91.9 [[Megahertz|MHz]]) for NCE stations only (called the [[reserved band]]), and channel 200 (87.9MHz) only for [[class D (radio)|class D]] NCE stations (not including [[translator (radio)|translator]]s) forced to move by a full-power station.

On the [[TV band]], individual channels are reserved, such that there is at least one in every area. In [[Canada]], the [[CRTC]] operates the FM band this way as wel, usually licensing at least one independent non-commercial station in addition to [[Canadian Broadcasting Corporation|CBC]] [[English language|English]] and/or [[French language|French]].

NCE stations may also operate on a non-reserved channel.</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
  <page>
    <title>Tomcat Catalina</title>
    <id>275674</id>
    <revision>
      <id>36492879</id>
      <timestamp>2006-01-24T12:28:09Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Doug Bell</username>
        <id>752893</id>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[computing]], '''Catalina''' is the name of the [[Servlet container]] of [[Jakarta Tomcat]] since version 4.x. It is developed under the [[Jakarta Project]] of the [[Apache Software Foundation]]. Tomcat implements [[Sun Microsystems]]'s specifications for [[Java servlet|Servlet]] and [[JavaServer Pages]] (JSP), which are important [[Java platform|Java]] based [[Web technologies]].

Tomcat's servlet container was redesigned as Catalina in Tomcat version 4.x. The architect for Catalina was [[Craig McClanahan]].

== External links ==
*[http://jakarta.apache.org/tomcat/ Jakarta Tomcat]
*[http://jakarta.apache.org/ The Apache Jakarta Project]

[[Category:Java enterprise platform]]

{{compu-soft-stub}}</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
  <page>
    <title>Augusta Reuss-Ebersdorf</title>
    <id>275675</id>
    <revision>
      <id>33675072</id>
      <timestamp>2006-01-03T02:24:26Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>FeanorStar7</username>
        <id>160806</id>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Artemisia.jpg|240px|right|thumb|'''Auguste of Reuss-Ebersdorf''' as ''Artemisia'', 1775,  painted by [[Johann Heinrich Tischbein]], sen., called: the Kasseler.]]

'''Countess Augusta Caroline Reuss zu Ebersdorf und Lobenstein''' ([[19 January ]] [[1757]] &amp;ndash; [[6 November]] [[1831]]), was the daughter of Count [[Heinrich XXIV Reuss zu Ebersdorf]] ([[1724]]-[[1779]]) and his wife Countess [[Karoline Ernestine zu Erbach-Schönberg]] ([[1727]]-[[1796]]).

She was born in [[Ebersdorf]]. She married, on [[13 June]] [[1777]], at Ebersdorf, [[Francis Frederick of Saxe-Coburg-Saalfield|Franz Friedrich, Duke of Saxe-Coburg-Saalfeld]].

Their children were:	
* Sophie (1778-1835)
* Antoinette (1779-1824)
* Juliane (1781-1860)
* [[Ernst I of Saxe-Coburg-Gotha|Ernst I]] (1784-1844)
* Ferdinand (1785-1851)
* [[Viktoria of Saxe-Coburg-Saalfeld|Viktoria]] (1786-1861)
* Marianne Charlotte (1788-1794)
* [[Leopold I of Belgium|Léopold I]] (1790-1865), King of the Belgians from 1831
* Maximilian (1792-1793)

Countess Augusta is the grandmother of both [[Victoria of the United Kingdom|Queen Victoria]] (through her mother [[Viktoria of Saxe-Coburg-Saalfeld|Viktoria]]) and her husband, [[Prince Albert of Saxe-Coburg-Gotha|Prince Albert]] (through his father [[Ernst I of Saxe-Coburg-Gotha|Ernst]]).  She died in [[Coburg]].

[[Category:1757 births|Reuss-Ebersdorf, Augusta]]
[[Category:1831 deaths|Reuss-Ebersdorf, Augusta]]

[[de:Auguste von Reuss-Ebersdorf]]
[[nl:Augusta van Reuss-Ebersdorf en Lobenstein]]</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
  <page>
    <title>Francis Frederick, Duke of Saxe-Coburg-Saalfeld</title>
    <id>275676</id>
    <revision>
      <id>33528069</id>
      <timestamp>2006-01-01T23:39:12Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Gdrbot</username>
        <id>263608</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>Robot-assisted disambiguation: Queen Victoria</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Franz Friedrich Anton, Duke of Saxe-Coburg-Saalfeld''' ([[15 July]] [[1750]] &amp;ndash; [[9 December ]] [[1806]]), was the son of [[Ernst Friedrich, Duke of Saxe-Coburg-Saalfeld]] ([[1724]]-[[1800]]) and his wife [[Sophia Antonia of Brunswick-Wolfenbüttel]] ([[1724]]-[[1802]]).

He married, on [[6 March]] [[1776]], at [[Hildburghausen]], Sophie of Saxe-Hildburghausen. She was born on [[22 February]] [[1760]] and died on [[28 October]] [[1776]], months after her wedding; there were no children born of this marriage.

He married, on [[13 June]] [[1777]], at [[Ebersdorf]], Countess [[Augusta Reuss-Ebersdorf|Auguste Reuss zu Ebersdorf und Lobenstein]].

Their children were:	
* Sophie ([[1778]]-[[1835]])
* Antoinette ([[1779]]-[[1824]])
* Juliane ([[1781]]-[[1860]])
* [[Ernst I of Saxe-Coburg-Gotha|Ernst I]] ([[1784]]-[[1844]]) father of [[Albert]]
* Ferdinand ([[1785]]-[[1851]]) father of [[Ferdinand II of Portugal]]
* [[Viktoria of Saxe-Coburg-Saalfeld|Viktoria]] ([[1786]]-[[1861]]), mother of [[Victoria of the United Kingdom|Queen Victoria]]
* Marianne Charlotte ([[1788]]-[[1794]])
* [[Léopold I of Belgium|Léopold I]] ([[1790]]-[[1865]]), first king of the [[Belgium|Belgians]]
* Maximilian ([[1792]]-[[1793]])

Duke Franz Friedrich is the grandfather of both [[Victoria of the United Kingdom|Queen Victoria]] (through her mother [[Viktoria of Saxe-Coburg-Saalfeld|Viktoria]]) and her husband, [[Prince Albert of Saxe-Coburg-Gotha|Prince Albert]] (through his father [[Ernst I of Saxe-Coburg-Gotha|Ernst]]).

His descendants established ruling houses in Belguim, Great Britain, Portugal and Bulgaria. His son Léopold ruled as [[Léopold I of Belgium]]. His grandchildren Victoria and Albert ruled Great Britain.  Another grandson Ferdinand, ruled as King-consort [[Ferdinand II of Portugal]]. Finally,  a great-grandson ruled as [[Ferdinand I of Bulgaria]].


[[Category:1750 births|Saxe-Coburg-Saalfield, Francis Frederick of]]
[[Category:1806 deaths|Saxe-Coburg-Saalfield, Francis Frederick of]]
[[Category:Dukes of Saxe-Coburg-Saalfeld]]

[[de:Franz (Sachsen-Coburg-Saalfeld)]]
[[nl:Frans van Saksen-Coburg-Saalfeld]]</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
