  <page>
    <title>Cole</title>
    <id>275794</id>
    <revision>
      <id>40893157</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-23T18:41:19Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Kvaks</username>
        <id>114658</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>etymology</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Cole''' can refer to several subjects:
* For the jazz singer, see [[Nat King Cole]].
* For the legendary and perhaps historical [[monarch|king]] of [[Wales]], see [[Old King Cole]].
* For either of the [[destroyer]]s of the [[United States Navy|U.S. Navy]], see [[USS Cole]].
* For various people with the [[surname]] Cole, see [[List of people by name: Col#Cole as surname]].
* For the [[University of Maryland, College Park]] basketball areana, see [[Cole Field House]].
* For the nineteenth century American artist, see [[Thomas Cole]]
* For the Oklahoma Congressperson, see [[Tom Cole]]
* For the American Singer and songwriter, see [[Paula Cole]]
* For the English journalist, economist and historian, see [[G. D. H. Cole]]
* For the English footballers [[Ashley Cole]], [[Joe Cole (footballer)|Joe Cole]], [[Andy Cole]] and [[Carlton Cole]]
* For the ''Friday Night SmackDown!'' announcer Michael Cole, see [[Michael Sean Coulthard]]

Cole is a common surname and may also be a first name (more so in USA). It means &quot;black&quot; in [[Old English]].

{{disambig}}</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
