        <id>24744</id>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">:''OMX is also the [[ticker symbol]] for [[OfficeMax]].''
----
{{Infobox_Company |
  company_name   = OMX AB |
  company_logo   = [[Image:OMX_logo.gif]] |
  company_type   = [[Public company|Public]] ([[OMX]]: ) |
  foundation = 2003 |
  company_slogan    = -- |
  location       = [[Stockholm]], [[Sweden]] |
  key_people     = [[Magnus Böcker]], CEO |
  products       = [[Stock exchange]] |
  homepage       = [http://www.omxgroup.com/ www.omxgroup.com] |
  industry       = [[Financial services]] |
  num_employees = 1,371 |
  revenue        = SEK 3,115 m (EUR 341 m) 
}}

'''OMX AB''' is a [[Sweden|Swedish]]-[[Finland|Finnish]] [[financial services]] company, formed in [[2003]] through a merger between '''OM AB''' and '''HEX plc'''. It has two divisions, OMX Exchanges, which operates six [[stock exchange]]s in the [[Nordic countries|Nordic]] and [[Baltic countries]], and OMX Technology, which develops and markets systems for financial transactions used by OMX Exchanges, as well as by other stock exchanges. The company is a world leader in financial instruments trading systems.

==History==

'''OM AB''' (''Optionsmarknaden'') was a [[futures exchange]] founded by [[Olof Stenhammar]] in the [[1980s]] to introduce trading in standardized [[option|option contracts]] in Sweden. OM acquired the [[Stockholm Stock Exchange]] in [[1998]] and unsuccessfully attempted acquisition of the [[London Stock Exchange]] in [[2001]].

On [[3 September]] [[2003]] the [[Helsinki Stock Exchange]] (HEX) merged with OM, and the joint company became '''OM HEX'''. On [[August 31]], [[2004]], the brand name of the company was changed to OMX.

== OMX Exchanges ==
*[[Copenhagen Stock Exchange]]
*[[Stockholm Stock Exchange]]
*[[Helsinki Stock Exchange]]
*[[Tallinn Stock Exchange]]
*[[Riga Stock Exchange]]
*[[Vilnius Stock Exchange]]

==See also==
*[[List of stock exchanges]]
*[[List of Swedish companies]]

== External links ==
*[http://www.omxgroup.com/ OMX] - Official site
*[http://www.omxgroup.com/campaigns/en/brandannouncment.aspx Press release on the OMX brand name]

[[Category:Companies of Sweden]]

[[da:OMX]]</text>
