    <title>Image:Brixham.hind.750pix.jpg</title>
    <id>275891</id>
    <revision>
      <id>16149381</id>
      <timestamp>2004-12-24T13:26:34Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>MarkSweep</username>
        <id>58666</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>refined tag</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">A replica of Sir Francis Drake's ship - the Golden Hind - lying permanently in Brixham Harbour.&lt;br&gt;

The original ship, with a crew of 80 sailors and 10 officers, circumnavigated the globe between 1577 and 1580.&lt;br&gt;
Five ships set out -  Pelican, Elizabeth, Swan, Marigold and Benedict.
During the voyage the Pelican was renamed the Golden Hind in honour of his friend Christopher Hatton whose  crest featured a hind (a deer).&lt;br&gt;
Sir Francis brought home looted gold, silver, jewels and cash worth 25 million pounds in today's (2003) money.&lt;br&gt;
Only two of the ships returned, the Golden Hind and the Elizabeth.

Taken by Adrian Pingstone in July 2003 and released to the public domain.
{{PD-user|Arpingstone}}</text>
    </revision>
