      <comment>dab</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Kortrijk aka Courtrai in Belgium Redvers.jpg|thumb|right|Central Kortrijk from the main square.]]
[[Image:Broeltorens.jpg|thumb|right|Broel towers]]
'''Kortrijk''' ([[French language|French]]: '''Courtrai''') is a city and municipality 
located in [[West Flanders]], [[Belgium]]. 

The city is situated on the [[River Lys]] 42 km (26 miles) southwest of [[Ghent]], at the map coordinates 50 50N 03 17E. It was founded by the [[Ancient Rome|Romans]], who called it ''Cortoriacum''. Kortrijk gained great importance as a centre of [[linen]] production during the [[Middle Ages]] and is still the largest producer of linen in western Europe. The [[Battle of the Golden Spurs]] ([[Dutch language|Dutch]]: ''Guldensporenslag'') took place near Kortrijk on [[July 11]], [[1302]], when the local [[Flemings|Flemish]] population mounted a successful uprising against the [[France|French]] rulers of Flanders. The chapel of the count (&quot;Gravenkapel&quot;) in the church of Our Lady (Onze-Lieve-Vrouwekerk) has a large number of golden spurs painted on the ceiling. Another reminder of Kortrijk's medieval history are the Broel towers and the small bridge in between spanning one arm of the river.

The wider municipality comprises the city of Kortrijk proper and the towns of [[Aalbeke]], [[Bellegem]], [[Bissegem]], [[Heule]], [[Kooigem]], [[Marke]] and [[Rollegem]]. On January 1st, 2005 Kortrijk had a total population of 73,625. The total area is 80.03 [[square kilometre|km&amp;sup2;]] which gives a [[population density]] of 919.96 inhabitants per km&amp;sup2;. 

The [[KULAK]], a department of the [[Katholieke Universiteit Leuven|Catholic University of Leuven]] is located in Kortrijk.

== Famous citizens ==
*[[Hendrik Conscience]], [[writer]]
*[[Stefaan De Clerck]], [[politician]] and [[mayor]] of Kortrijk
*[[Ernest Gambart]], art publisher
*[[Carl de Keyzer]], [[photographer]]
*[[Pierre de La Rue]], [[Renaissance]] [[composer]]
*[[Ann De Meulemeester]], [[fashion designer]]
*[[Guido Gezelle]], [[poet]]
*[[Piet Goddaer]], singer of [[Ozark Henry]]
*[[Xavier Malisse]], [[tennis]] player
*[[Morris (comics)|Morris]], creator of [[Lucky Luke]]
*[[Jan Palfyn]] (1650-1730), [[Physician|doctor]], [[surgeon]] and inventor of the [[forceps]]
*[[Louis Robbe]] (1806-1887), [[painter]] 
*[[Roeland Savery]] (1576-1639), painter
*[[Stijn Streuvels]] (1871-1969), writer
*[[Vincent Van Quickenborne]], [[Belgium|Belgian]] [[Secretary of State]]

==External links==
*[http://www.kortrijk.be Official website] - Information available in [[Dutch language|Dutch]], [[French language|French]], [[English language|English]] and [[German language|German]]

[[Category:Municipalities of West Flanders]]
