  <page>
    <title>Sticker art</title>
    <id>275977</id>
    <revision>
      <id>37103204</id>
      <timestamp>2006-01-28T18:19:43Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Ceyockey</username>
        <id>150564</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>[[USPS]]=&gt;[[United States Postal Service]]</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Sticker art''' is a form of [[street art]] in which the [[message]] is conveyed by stickers. Sticker art is most noticeable in well-trafficked urban areas. Stickers may promote a political agenda (such as the anti-war and  anti-[[George W. Bush]] stickers below), comment on a policy or issue (such as the [[Massachusetts Institute of Technology|MIT]] sticker below), or comprise an avant-garde art campaign (see [[This Is A Heavy Product]] and [[Obey Giant]]). 

Sticker art is popular with [[teenager]]s and within the [[skateboarding]] subculture, due mostly to ready availability of supplies. Sometimes, unintentional sticker art can occur, with unconventional discards of free stickers, for example free stickers from [[voting Booth| voting booth]]s, retail stickers, [[United States Postal Service]] labels, and stickers acquired from school drug-awareness programs. Sticker art is considered a subcategory of [[postmodern art]].

{| border=&quot;0&quot; cellpadding=&quot;2&quot; cellspacing=&quot;2&quot; align=&quot;center&quot;
|-
|valign=&quot;top&quot;|[[Image:bush-sticker-nyc04.jpg|thumb|''Protest sticker on the [[Manhattan Bridge]] in [[New York City]]. Image: U.S. President [[George W. Bush]]. Text: &quot;Elect a madman / you get madness.&quot;'']]
|valign=&quot;top&quot;|[[Image:French anti-war sticker.jpg|thumb|[[Anti-war]] sticker in [[Paris]], [[France]]]]
|-
|valign=&quot;top&quot;|[[Image:Mit-card-reader-sticker.jpeg.jpg|thumb|''Satirical protest sticker on a keycard reader at [[MIT]]. Text: &quot;All activity monitored for your protection. MIT Card Office. A division of the Department of Homeland Security.&quot;'']]
|valign=&quot;top&quot;|[[Image:Propaganda política.jpg|thumb|''Satirical sticker protest candidate to mayor in [[Cuiaba]] [[Brazil]].]]
|-
|}

==See also==
* [[culture jamming]]
* [[street art]]
* [[graffiti]]

== External links ==

* [http://www.pop.ac/ pop.ac], art with stickers - since 1987, let's stick together - sticker happenings, divine sticker art - connects you with god.
* [http://www.bunnymatic.com/sightings/ bunnymatic.com/sightings], examples of 'bunnymatic' stickers in various locations.
* [http://www.urbanize.org/ urbanize.org], examples of sticker and other graffiti art.
* [http://www.peelzine.com/  sticker site.
* [http://nickm.com/implementation/ Implementation], a sticker novel including archive photos of stickers around the world
* [http://www.yourmumrang.co.uk/ Your Mum Rang]UK Sticker campaign kickstarted by [http://www.schudio.co.uk Chu]
* [http://www.bomit.com/ bomit.com], street art sticker portal offering free stickers to visitors.
*[http://www.kolahstudio.com/Graffiti.htm Todays Iranian Stencil and Graffiti movement]
* [http://www.bldd.nl/ BLDD collects information concerning contemporary art, street art, urban art as you wish.]Updated weekly

{{art-stub}}

{{commons|:Category:Stencil}}

[[Category:Graffiti and unauthorised signage]]

[[pt:Sticker art]]</text>
