  <page>
    <title>Randonneurs USA</title>
    <id>276027</id>
    <revision>
      <id>26409043</id>
      <timestamp>2005-10-25T03:01:47Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Vclaw</username>
        <id>235019</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>Category:Cycling organisations</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Randonneurs USA''' or ''RUSA'' is the [[Audax Club Parisien]] sanctioned [[brevet (bicycle)|brevet]] coordinating organization for the [[United States]].  U.S. [[Cyclist]]s riding in the [[Paris-Brest-Paris]] qualify for the event through RUSA.  RUSA also promotes &quot;randonneuring&quot; within the U.S..

[[Randonneur]]ing is a style of bicycle riding that requires covering long-distances over an unmarked course of challenging terrain within a generously allotted time period of almost continuous riding.  As [[Randonneur|randonneurs]], riders do not compete against their fellow cyclists, but only against their own personal best, the weather and the mind's desire for sleep.  Skills in self-sufficiency, bicycle mechanics, night-riding and endurance are all valued over ability to cycle at racing speeds or with racing strategies.

==External links==
*[http://www.rusa.org RUSA]
*[http://www.audax-club-parisien.com/ Audax Club Parisien]

[[Category:Cycling organisations]]</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
