  <page>
    <title>Brat Pack (movies)</title>
    <id>276088</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41557123</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-28T03:21:49Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>68.5.246.25</ip>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">:''For other uses, see [[Brat Pack disambiguation]].''

The '''&quot;Brat Pack&quot;''' was a group of young actors and actresses that became famous in the [[1980s]] and frequently appeared in teen-oriented films together. The name &quot;Brat Pack&quot; came from a [[1985]] cover story in ''New York'' magazine by David Blum ([[June 10]] [[1985]], pp. 40-47). The term is a play on the [[Rat Pack]] from the 1960s. Popular films that featured members of the &quot;Brat Pack&quot; include:
  
*''[[The Outsiders (novel)|The Outsiders]]'' (1983)
*''[[Sixteen Candles]]'' (1984)
*''[[The Breakfast Club]]'' (1985)
*''[[St. Elmo's Fire (movie)|St. Elmo's Fire]]'' (1985)
*''[[Weird Science]]'' (1985)
*''[[About Last Night (film)|About Last Night]]'' (1986)
*''[[Pretty in Pink]]'' (1986)
*''[[The Lost Boys]]'' (1987)
*''[[Young Guns]]'' (1988)

The Eight Core Members of the Brat Pack members are:
*[[Emilio Estevez]]
*[[Anthony Michael Hall]]
*[[Rob Lowe]]
*[[Andrew McCarthy]]
*[[Demi Moore]]
*[[Judd Nelson]]
*[[Molly Ringwald]] 
*[[Ally Sheedy]]

Other actors could be considered auxiliary members of the Pack:  
*[[Kevin Bacon]]
*[[Matthew Broderick]]
*[[Tom Cruise]] 
*[[John Cusack]]
*[[Matt Dillon]]
*[[Robert Downey, Jr.]]
*[[Jami Gertz]]
*[[Jennifer Grey]]
*[[C. Thomas Howell]]
*[[Diane Lane]] 
*[[Mary Stuart Masterson]]
*[[Charlie Sheen]]
*[[James Spader]]
*[[Kiefer Sutherland]]
*[[Patrick Swayze]]
*[[Mare Winningham]]
*[[Michael J. Fox]] 

Frequent directors of Brat Pack films were: 
*[[John Hughes (film director)|John Hughes]] 
*[[Joel Schumacher]]

==External link==
*http://www.thebratpacksite.com

[[Category:American actors]]
[[Category:Entertainment cliques]]

[[de:Brat Pack]]
[[nl:Brat Pack]]
[[ja:ブラット・パック]]
[[sv:Brat Pack]]</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
